    <h3 class="sev sev-high">▲ High (2)</h3>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-d9443086f45eab93">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-high">▲ High</span>
        <strong>tools/list page 1 does not match the schema</strong>
        <span class="muted">schema.tools_list_valid</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>(result): &#39;resultType&#39; is a required property</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;page&#34;: 1,
    &#34;problems&#34;: [
      &#34;(result): &#39;resultType&#39; is a required property&#34;
    ]
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">d9443086f45eab93</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">tools-list:page-1</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/server/tools#listing-tools</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>Clients parse tools/list with the official schema. A tool without inputSchema or a result with the wrong shape breaks every client that validates strictly.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Return tools/list results that validate against the version&#39;s schema.json.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding d9443086f45eab93</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding d9443086f45eab93">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-dd7555e6e4c0ad3a">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-high">▲ High</span>
        <strong>server/discover result is incomplete</strong>
        <span class="muted">protocol.discover_implemented</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>resultType is missing</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;problems&#34;: [
      &#34;resultType is missing&#34;
    ]
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">dd7555e6e4c0ad3a</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">discover:incomplete</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/server/discover</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>Clients detect a server&#39;s era and supported versions with server/discover. A modern-capable server without it looks like a legacy server and is driven with the wrong protocol.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Implement server/discover and return supportedVersions, capabilities, resultType, ttlMs and cacheScope.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding dd7555e6e4c0ad3a</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding dd7555e6e4c0ad3a">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    
    <h3 class="sev sev-medium">◆ Medium (2)</h3>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-257b54e714b7bfc5">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-medium">◆ Medium</span>
        <strong>Unresolvable or remote $ref: notes_create</strong>
        <span class="muted">schema.refs_resolvable on notes_create</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>inputSchema: #/$defs/missing is unresolvable</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;problems&#34;: [
      &#34;inputSchema: #/$defs/missing is unresolvable&#34;
    ]
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">257b54e714b7bfc5</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">refs:notes_create</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/server/tools#tool</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>A $ref that points nowhere makes the schema unusable. A remote $ref makes clients fetch URLs the server chose, which leaks requests and invites SSRF.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Inline remote definitions under $defs and make every $ref point inside the schema.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding 257b54e714b7bfc5</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding 257b54e714b7bfc5">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-c9276d64428bb6da">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-medium">◆ Medium</span>
        <strong>Results without resultType</strong>
        <span class="muted">protocol.result_type_present</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>357 result(s) lacked resultType (methods: resources/list, server/discover, tools/call, tools/list)</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;count&#34;: 357,
    &#34;methods&#34;: [
      &#34;resources/list&#34;,
      &#34;server/discover&#34;,
      &#34;tools/call&#34;,
      &#34;tools/list&#34;
    ],
    &#34;trace_seq&#34;: [
      1,
      3,
      5,
      7,
      9
    ]
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">c9276d64428bb6da</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">result-type:missing</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/schema#result</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>resultType tells a client whether a result is complete or needs more input. Without it, clients cannot tell a finished result from an input request.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Include resultType (&#34;complete&#34; or &#34;input_required&#34;) in every result.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding c9276d64428bb6da</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding c9276d64428bb6da">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    
    <h3 class="sev sev-low">● Low (1)</h3>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-b227f850ebe28aa0">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-low">● Low</span>
        <strong>Read tools withstand concurrent bursts</strong>
        <span class="muted">operability.burst_resilient on notes_get</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>garbled tool result: (result): &#39;resultType&#39; is a required property</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;concurrent_calls&#34;: 50,
    &#34;problems&#34;: [
      &#34;garbled tool result: (result): &#39;resultType&#39; is a required property&#34;
    ],
    &#34;reproduced_crash&#34;: false
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">b227f850ebe28aa0</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">burst:notes_get</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/server/tools#error-handling</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>A short traffic spike should yield usable results or explicit rate-limit errors.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Bound concurrency and return well-formed results or rate-limit errors with retry guidance.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding b227f850ebe28aa0</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding b227f850ebe28aa0">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    
    <h3 class="sev sev-info">○ Info (2)</h3>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-513f8a442622ff40">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-info">○ Info</span>
        <strong>Some input schemas are not strict</strong>
        <span class="muted">schema.input_schema_strict</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>15 tool(s) allow additional properties or list no required parameters.</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;count&#34;: 15,
    &#34;tools&#34;: [
      &#34;notes_create&#34;,
      &#34;notes_update&#34;,
      &#34;notes_delete&#34;,
      &#34;notes_get&#34;,
      &#34;notes_list&#34;,
      &#34;search_notes&#34;,
      &#34;fetch_url&#34;,
      &#34;read_file&#34;,
      &#34;write_file&#34;,
      &#34;query_db&#34;,
      &#34;git_log&#34;,
      &#34;slow_report&#34;,
      &#34;purge_notes&#34;,
      &#34;call_backend&#34;,
      &#34;long_export&#34;
    ]
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">513f8a442622ff40</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">input-schema-strict:summary</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/server/tools#tool</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>Schemas that forbid extra properties and list required ones reject malformed calls early. Loose ones accept whatever a model invents.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Set &#34;additionalProperties&#34;: false and list required parameters.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding 513f8a442622ff40</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding 513f8a442622ff40">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    <details class="finding" id="f-9a6ec162a9613023">
      <summary><span class="sev sev-info">○ Info</span>
        <strong>Startup latency is recorded</strong>
        <span class="muted">operability.startup_time</span></summary>
      <div class="body">
        <p>First successful response after 623.6 ms.</p>
        
        <pre>{
    &#34;startup_ms&#34;: 623.59912109375
  }</pre>
        <dl>
          <dt>Finding id</dt><dd class="mono">9a6ec162a9613023</dd>
          <dt>Case</dt><dd class="mono">startup</dd>
          <dt>Spec</dt><dd>2026-07-28/basic/lifecycle#initialization</dd>
          <dt>Why it matters</dt><dd>Time to the first successful response describes cold-start operability.</dd>
          <dt>How to fix</dt><dd>Investigate cold starts longer than 30 seconds.</dd>
          <dt>Reproduce</dt>
          <dd class="repro"><code>probe repro report.json --finding 9a6ec162a9613023</code>
            <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="probe repro report.json --finding 9a6ec162a9613023">Copy</button></dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </details>
    
    
    
  </section>
  
